{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Words of his mouth.</b> Far be it that the wise man be one of mere speech, when all the words that proceed from his mouth are grace. And the fool destroys himself by his speech. And he said, <b>will swallow him up</b> — singular tongue, like the matter of <i>flies of death</i>, <i>sun</i>, <i>moon</i>, <i>stood</i>, <i>his dwelling</i>."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:57.000422327Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}